    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d735">

                <pb facs="0841" n="749" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg749"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/10524</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bundy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-27T16:00:00-00:43">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 27, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 28, 9.54 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>French Chargé d’Affaires here informed Legation yesterday that Liberian
                    Government had notified him in a communication dated June 25 that French
                    wireless station may be reopened.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bundy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
